{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks","id":798165,"title":"[3E] Immaculate Martial Arts, Dragon-Blooded and mortal Monks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-02T01:48:37-08:00","id":798165,"title":"[3E] Immaculate Martial Arts, Dragon-Blooded and mortal Monks","content":"Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I've got a few questions regarding Immaculate Martial Arts in 3E. The core book doesn't expand on them, but I feel they're too deeply tied to the Immaculate Order and the Realm's influence to be forgotten.<br /> <br /> So, I still struggle with a couple points :<br /> - can mortal Monks using Immaculate Martial Arts be a threat to spirits? Since there are theoretically no more Essence-wielding mortals, I'd have to say no, but that would mean that the spirit-policing done by the Order is exclusively handled by the Dragon-Blooded Monks, and there can't be all that many of them (relatively speaking)<br /> - even without Immaculate MA, would mortal Monks negotiate with spirits, considering they have the weight of the Order behind them?<br /> - 3E seems to do away with the Terrestrial vs Celestial Martial Arts by using the Terrestrial and Mastery keywords, but I really liked that distinction<br /> <br /> So far, I've ruled the following :<br /> - The Five Glorious Dragon Styles are taught to Dragon-Blooded Monks and those who attend the Cloister of Wisdom ; they can't be used efficiently by Celestial Exalted because they're too elementally aspected<br /> - The Five-Dragon Path is a lesser, synthetic taught to Dragon-Blooded outside the order who can't/don't want to spend as much time studying a style<br /> - Mortal Monks are taught a lightweight version of the Five-Dragon Path, since they can't use Essence ; some of them may be taught the Essence-less version of non-Immaculate Martial Arts if they show promise (mostly so that my Solar PCs can grab an Immaculate background if they want)<br /> <br /> How do you guys handle Immaculate MA in 3E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9458-boz0","name":"boz0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9458_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T01:50:36-08:00","id":798166,"title":"","content":"I'm just curious if there's like a specialty Merit that Dragon Bloods can take that lets them ignore the effects of the Terrestrial Keyword with a Martial Arts Style.<br /> <br /> I mean, when I was running a game with the Leaked Document, there was one of each Aspect Monk. And I can tell you, from my test of smashing each Monk against a Solar PC... The Five Dragon Styles, at least, are quite lethal. A Solar will need to work for their victory... And if multiple monks can start double-teaming a Solar, then shit gets real.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for the Five-Dragon Path, since I was only really aware that it existed in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 01-02-2016, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T02:26:14-08:00","id":798173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>boz0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks#post798165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I've got a few questions regarding Immaculate Martial Arts in 3E. The core book doesn't expand on them, but I feel they're too deeply tied to the Immaculate Order and the Realm's influence to be forgotten.<br /> <br /> So, I still struggle with a couple points :<br /> - can mortal Monks using Immaculate Martial Arts be a threat to spirits? Since there are theoretically no more Essence-wielding mortals, I'd have to say no, but that would mean that the spirit-policing done by the Order is exclusively handled by the Dragon-Blooded Monks, and there can't be all that many of them (relatively speaking)</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding, while the non-Exalted non-Exalted might learn the relevant Martial Arts skill, they now cannot use Supernatural Martial Arts charms themselves. Which is something of a pity - I would have liked mortals to gain <i>some</i> game mechanical benefit for learning a Martial Art just to build slightly more interesting mooks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - even without Immaculate MA, would mortal Monks negotiate with spirits, considering they have the weight of the Order behind them? </div> </div> </div>I presume so, though presumably they will only be sent to deal with the weaker spirit. &quot;Behave, or the temple master will come and deal with you!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - 3E seems to do away with the Terrestrial vs Celestial Martial Arts by using the Terrestrial and Mastery keywords, but I really liked that distinction </div> </div> </div>I am actually glad about that, since that means it's now possible to find a sifu for what used to be a &quot;Celestial&quot; Martial Arts without finding an actual Celestial Martial Artist. Solars being just plain better at <i>expressing</i> a Martial Art works for me.<br /> <br /> I am still rather curious how Sidereal Martial Arts will be handled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/sunkencastles\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Sunken Castles, Evil Poodles</b></a> is creating Public Domain translations of German folklore!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://german-geek.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>A German Geek</b></a> - my gaming blog!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10279-j\u00fcrgen-hubert","name":"J\u00fcrgen Hubert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T02:42:28-08:00","id":798179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>boz0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks#post798165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I've got a few questions regarding Immaculate Martial Arts in 3E. The core book doesn't expand on them, but I feel they're too deeply tied to the Immaculate Order and the Realm's influence to be forgotten.<br /> <br /> So, I still struggle with a couple points :<br /> - can mortal Monks using Immaculate Martial Arts be a threat to spirits? Since there are theoretically no more Essence-wielding mortals, I'd have to say no, but that would mean that the spirit-policing done by the Order is exclusively handled by the Dragon-Blooded Monks, and there can't be all that many of them (relatively speaking)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, mortal monks in 2nd ed could do a few extra points of damage with Five-Dragon (the style they normally learnt, since the Immaculate styles were impossible) and get a few extra points of soak, so I don't feel there's a big drop in their capabilities compared to before.<br /> It's still a case of highly motivated, highly skilled kung-fu guys turning up and punching your priests, and threatening to call their DB boss if you call your boss. Most of the gods they push around are the weaker terrestrial gods.<br /> <br /> Though... in 2nd ed, if a ghost-blood, demon-blood or god-blood was born in an Immaculate-controlled area, they'd normally be taken off their parents and raised as monks, then used as exorcists (as they have useful powers for it) when they grow up. So maybe that's still the case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - even without Immaculate MA, would mortal Monks negotiate with spirits, considering they have the weight of the Order behind them? </div> </div> </div>I'd think so. It's still going to be mortal monks only negotiating with the local small gods; things like the god of a large city will require a DB's touch. But the god of a small river who demands the villagers worship him? That's what a team of mortal monks will deal with.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind these aren't mortal schlubs. Chumps who become monks sweep the temple. The guys who deal with small gods are professional exorcists and spirit-wranglers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - The Five-Dragon Path is a lesser, synthetic taught to Dragon-Blooded outside the order who can't/don't want to spend as much time studying a style </div> </div> </div>That was the case in 2nd ed... I'm curious as to whether Five-Dragon will still exist or not now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Mortal Monks are taught a lightweight version of the Five-Dragon Path, since they can't use Essence ; some of them may be taught the Essence-less version of non-Immaculate Martial Arts if they show promise (mostly so that my Solar PCs can grab an Immaculate background if they want) </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the way I intend to handle it (hasn't really come up so far).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T04:26:23-08:00","id":798200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798166#post798166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just curious if there's like a specialty Merit that Dragon Bloods can take that lets them ignore the effects of the Terrestrial Keyword with a Martial Arts Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's been said by the devs that Immaculate Styles give more to Dragon-Blooded who are initiated into the higher mysteries of the Order than they do to Solars (or at least other Celestials), even. I'm not sure what that means, though, or how it will be handled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T04:47:58-08:00","id":798205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>*End</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798200#post798200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's been said by the devs that Immaculate Styles give more to Dragon-Blooded who are initiated into the higher mysteries of the Order than they do to Solars (or at least other Celestials), even. I'm not sure what that means, though, or how it will be handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Immaculate Styles were developed specifically for DB, I'd just guess the high-end Charms require the appropriate Element and therefore can't be used as intended by other Celestials.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9458-boz0","name":"boz0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9458_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T05:01:01-08:00","id":798207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798179#post798179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still going to be mortal monks only negotiating with the local small gods; things like the god of a large city will require a DB's touch. But the god of a small river who demands the villagers worship him? That's what a team of mortal monks will deal with.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind these aren't mortal schlubs. Chumps who become monks sweep the temple. The guys who deal with small gods are professional exorcists and spirit-wranglers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to make another category besides the DB Monks and the mortal Monks, and I want the mortal Monks to be worthy of the respect the order inspires.<br /> <br /> For now, and at least until the Dragon-Blooded splat is released, I'll also give mortal Monks a specific technique (either a pseudo-Charm or a Thaumaturgy ritual enacted through martial arts) that allows them to do minor damage to an immaterial spirit. Not enough to make a single Monk a real threat to any but the smallest spirits, but enough to make a small group of mortal Monks a significant annoyance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9458-boz0","name":"boz0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9458_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T06:07:31-08:00","id":798223,"title":"","content":"&quot;Being a threat to a spirit&quot; does not require punching them while they are immaterial. Destroying shrines and making impassioned speeches to would-be worshippers requires no supernatural badassery.<br /> <br /> Also, if I recall correctly, spirits can no longer just reflexively dematerialize or Hurry Home to avoid an attack - it takes a whole turn in which mortals can beat on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T06:42:17-08:00","id":798229,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Immaculate Order openly accepts some Exigents as representatives or agents, if not proper monks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T09:16:44-08:00","id":798286,"title":"","content":"Well, given the Exigents are seem to be actually be accepted by the Order as chosen by gods, so there's room in to accept them as monks. They weren't worthy of being chosen by the Immaculate Dragons, but they aren't demon-possessed. I'd suppose that the mightiest ones would be kick-ass operatives (on the level of celestial exalted), but there would be a very clear ceiling for them. One should not overdue this and make all the kick-ass monks Exigents, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T09:50:48-08:00","id":798300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>boz0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798205#post798205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd just guess the high-end Charms require the appropriate Element and therefore can't be used as intended by other Celestials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given Solars are The Best At Everything and Sidereals are The Best At Kung-Fu, I really doubt this will (or even should) be a Thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798166#post798166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, when I was running a game with the Leaked Document, there was one of each Aspect Monk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider it kind of a travesty that all 5 monks didn't make it into the backer doc. Certainly something of less value could be cut for 2 iconic antagonists!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 01-02-2016, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T11:07:24-08:00","id":798322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798300#post798300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider it kind of a travesty that all 5 monks didn't make it into the backer doc. Certainly something of less value could be cut for 2 iconic antagonists!</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a terrible shame, but on the other hand it seems a bit wasteful to spend that much antagonist space on Dragon-Bloods when they're going to be the first Exalt to get full rules. Once What Fire Has Wrought comes out we won't really need Immaculate monk antagonists, but we will still need all the other stuff in the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T12:15:11-08:00","id":798346,"title":"","content":"Everyone should check out the exorcist in the antagonist chapter of third Ed. That's how mortal monks kick spirit ass.<br /> <br /> Edit: I know that his abilities only target ghosts, but it's a good example of how trained and spiritually knowledgable monks can use mystical shit to fight supernatural things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 01-02-2016, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T12:31:06-08:00","id":798352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798322#post798322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a terrible shame, but on the other hand it seems a bit wasteful to spend that much antagonist space on Dragon-Bloods when they're going to be the first Exalt to get full rules. Once What Fire Has Wrought comes out we won't really need Immaculate monk antagonists, but we will still need all the other stuff in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the part of me that gets twitchy when table experience levels are uneven.<br /> <br /> Or don't. That part of me is overly nitpicky and pedantic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T21:50:11-08:00","id":799015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798322#post798322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is a terrible shame, but on the other hand it seems a bit wasteful to spend that much antagonist space on Dragon-Bloods when they're going to be the first Exalt to get full rules. Once What Fire Has Wrought comes out we won't really need Immaculate monk antagonists, but we will still need all the other stuff in the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second. Exigents first, then Dragon-Blooded. Which means we're probably looking at 2017, bare minimum, especially considering the core isn't even out yet.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T22:03:24-08:00","id":799048,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'm pretty sure Dragonblood is out first, that's why they've already started writing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T23:13:00-08:00","id":799077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=799015#post799015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second. Exigents first, then Dragon-Blooded. Which means we're probably looking at 2017, bare minimum, especially considering the core isn't even out yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the DB book is next. Check the Monday Meeting notes: the Dragon-Blood book is in second draft. The Exigent book has not been started.<br /> <br /> Doing surveys of RPG fans is hard, but the last I saw showed that Solars and DBs are the most popular splats and no other splat hasa significant following.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T23:41:12-08:00","id":799084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khantalas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=798229#post798229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the Immaculate Order openly accepts some Exigents as representatives or agents, if not proper monks.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game they can become agents, though this is a matter of some remark and contention amongst the more religiously conservative Immaculates. More realpolitik-oriented members are far more open to the idea of supplementing their ranks with as much might as they can muster, and some are even open to treating with Exigents as de-facto equals (despite Immaculate doctrine's teachings on the pre-eminence of DB's). The Exigents, for their part, gain safety from Wyld Hunts as well as access to some of the power of the Immaculate order and the attendant material and social benefits thereof (though they're typically treated as the outsiders they are). <br /> <br /> As for the topic of the thread, I'd be curious to see what other folks' homebrew QC-appropriate Immaculate charms might look like. My party has been doing a masterful job of steering clear of the Wyld Hunt, but they just raised their profile fairly substantially, which may well result in some mystical kung-fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T23:44:51-08:00","id":799088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=799077#post799077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the DB book is next. Check the Monday Meeting notes: the Dragon-Blood book is in second draft. The Exigent book has not been started.<br /> <br /> Doing surveys of RPG fans is hard, but the last I saw showed that Solars and DBs are the most popular splats and no other splat hasa significant following.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! I had thought Exigents were second.<br /> <br /> Thanks to everyone who corrected me. That's on me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T23:52:48-08:00","id":799099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=799077#post799077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the DB book is next. Check the Monday Meeting notes: the Dragon-Blood book is in second draft. The Exigent book has not been started.<br /> <br /> Doing surveys of RPG fans is hard, but the last I saw showed that Solars and DBs are the most popular splats and no other splat hasa significant following.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I saw that survey.<br /> <br /> And it was less &quot;Solars and DBs are most popular&quot; and more &quot;Most Exalted groups are all Solars and the next biggest are all DBs&quot;... Which a friend of mine noted COULD be attributed to them having some of the more functional charmsets of 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T00:28:23-08:00","id":799147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=799099#post799099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I saw that survey.<br /> <br /> And it was less &quot;Solars and DBs are most popular&quot; and more &quot;Most Exalted groups are all Solars and the next biggest are all DBs&quot;... Which a friend of mine noted COULD be attributed to them having some of the more functional charmsets of 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also DBs are the largest antagonist splat and the one that your PCs will most commonly encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T00:30:06-08:00","id":799149,"title":"","content":"And also the one they will have as their most common Exalted allies, in all likelihood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T00:31:35-08:00","id":799151,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure a functional Charmset is the opposite of the situation with 2e Dragon-Blooded by many accounts.<br /> <br /> They were always the second most popular, to be honest. We got Aspect Books and <b>Outcastes </b>in 1e, and <i>The </i><b>Thousand Correct Actions </b>which no other splat really getting similar supplementary support. And the Realm's civil war was the theme of the boardgame they did. Terrestrial Exalted, despite attempts in 2e to make folks think otherwise.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T01:39:17-08:00","id":799167,"title":"","content":"I've played about 6 Dragonblood games, and about 5 Solar games (some of whom had a few Lunars, and very occasionally had something else). I've played 1 Lunar game that wasn't very long, 1 Infernal game and 1 Alchemical game that both lasted about 5 sessions, and an Abyssal game that lasted 1 whole session.<br /> I've never played a Sidereal (though I'd like to).<br /> <br /> Talking to others, this experience doesn't seem particularly unusual.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Dragonblood charm set is actually reasonably okay; it has a lot of issues that are just easy to ignore (like the wrong steps in step resolution). Honestly, I felt that playing DBs worked better than playing Solars in a lot of ways, because there was no perfect spam. Of course, this relied on the ST avoiding having you fight people who could use multi-attack charms with grand goremauls, but I didn't find it particularly lethal. I've played about 7 DBs, and only 3 of them died (one to a grand goremaul in an argument about Mariachi, one to the Silent Wind of Adorjan, and one because she was punched by Walker in Darkness after spending 3 turns grappling him).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-03-2016, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T03:54:27-08:00","id":799408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/798165-3e-immaculate-martial-arts-dragon-blooded-and-mortal-monks?p=799167#post799167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, this relied on the ST avoiding having you fight people who could use multi-attack charms with grand goremauls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is more problematic than it sounds when you know those people can be other Dragon-Blooded rather than Melee focused Solar bullshit.<br /> My own personal issue were undodgable/unblockable attacks which, once again were readily attainable in a DB game if you knew where to look.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}